From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 11:49:47 +0200
Subject: media: hm5065: Report the mounting from the device tree

The sensor knows how it is mounted only because the device tree says
so, and nothing passed that on: no V4L2_CID_CAMERA_ORIENTATION, no
V4L2_CID_CAMERA_SENSOR_ROTATION, so a viewfinder had to keep a table
of boards.

Same two lines the gc2145 and the ov5640 already have. Absent
properties still create no controls, so this changes nothing on a
device tree that does not describe the mounting.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c b/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/hm5065.c
@@ -1359,6 +1359,7 @@ static int hm5065_init_controls(struct hm5065_dev *sensor)
 	const struct v4l2_ctrl_ops *ops = &hm5065_ctrl_ops;
 	struct hm5065_ctrls *ctrls = &sensor->ctrls;
 	struct v4l2_ctrl_handler *hdl = &ctrls->handler;
+	struct v4l2_fwnode_device_properties props;
 	u8 wb_max = 0;
 	u64 wb_mask = 0;
 	unsigned int i;
@@ -1483,6 +1484,14 @@ static int hm5065_init_controls(struct hm5065_dev *sensor)
 					  V4L2_CID_TEST_PATTERN_RED + i,
 					  0, 1023, 1, 0);
 
+	ret = v4l2_fwnode_device_parse(&sensor->i2c_client->dev, &props);
+	if (ret)
+		goto free_ctrls;
+
+	ret = v4l2_ctrl_new_fwnode_properties(hdl, ops, &props);
+	if (ret)
+		goto free_ctrls;
+
 	if (hdl->error) {
 		ret = hdl->error;
 		goto free_ctrls;
-- 
